{"name":"Vintage Glass","hex":"#cbd8b9","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"vintage","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The yield of grapes or wine from a vineyard or district during one season.","Wine, especially high-quality, identified as to year and vineyard or district of origin."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or relating to a vintage, or to wine identified by a specific vintage.","Having an enduring appeal; high-quality."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vintage"},{"term":"glass","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An amorphous solid, often transparent substance, usually made by melting silica sand with various additives (for most purposes, a mixture of soda, potash and lime is added).","Any amorphous solid (one without a regular crystal lattice)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To fit with glass; to glaze.","To enclose in glass."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glass"}],"entries":[{"title":"Vintage","blocks":[{"text":"In winemaking, vintage is the process of picking grapes to create wine. A vintage wine is one made from grapes that were all, or primarily, grown and harvested in a single specified year. In certain wines, it can denote quality, as in Port wine, where Port houses make and declare vintage Port in their best years. From this tradition, a common, though not strictly correct, usage applies the term to any wine that is perceived to be particularly old or of a particularly high quality."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Cup_vintage_Cdm_Paris_320_n1.jpg/330px-Cup_vintage_Cdm_Paris_320_n1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vintage","wikidata":"Q1975981"},{"title":"Glass","blocks":[{"text":"Glass is an amorphous (non-crystalline) solid. Because it is often transparent and chemically inert, glass has found widespread practical, technological, and decorative use in window panes, tableware, and optics. Some common objects made of glass are named after the material, e.g., a \"glass\" for drinking, \"glasses\" for vision correction, and a \"magnifying glass\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Fassade_Wilhelmstrasse_65%2C_Berlin-Mitte%2C_160417%2C_ako.jpg/330px-Fassade_Wilhelmstrasse_65%2C_Berlin-Mitte%2C_160417%2C_ako.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glass","wikidata":"Q11469"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/The_Vintagers_after_a_Miniature_of_the_Dialogues_de_Saint_Gregoire_Thirteenth_Century_Manuscript_of_the_Royal_Library_of_Brussels.png/500px-The_Vintagers_after_a_Miniature_of_the_Dialogues_de_Saint_Gregoire_Thirteenth_Century_Manuscript_of_the_Royal_Library_of_Brussels.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/The_Vintagers_after_a_Miniature_of_the_Dialogues_de_Saint_Gregoire_Thirteenth_Century_Manuscript_of_the_Royal_Library_of_Brussels.png/1280px-The_Vintagers_after_a_Miniature_of_the_Dialogues_de_Saint_Gregoire_Thirteenth_Century_Manuscript_of_the_Royal_Library_of_Brussels.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/The_Vintagers_after_a_Miniature_of_the_Dialogues_de_Saint_Gregoire_Thirteenth_Century_Manuscript_of_the_Royal_Library_of_Brussels.png/500px-The_Vintagers_after_a_Miniature_of_the_Dialogues_de_Saint_Gregoire_Thirteenth_Century_Manuscript_of_the_Royal_Library_of_Brussels.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Vintagers, after a miniature of the \"Dialogues de Saint Gregoire\" (13th century)—manuscript of the Royal Library of Belgium","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Vintagers_after_a_Miniature_of_the